course: dictionary
lesson: 6560
title: Nicely: two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Nicely is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done. It has two main meanings. The first is in a pleasant, kind or polite way: «ask nicely» means ask with «please» and a polite voice.
explain: The second meaning is well, in a good or satisfactory way: «the cake turned out nicely» means the cake came out well. To choose the right meaning, look at the words around nicely. Is someone being polite, or is something going well?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Strict parents often find a middle way if you ask politely» still makes sense, so nicely means politely here.
fact: Nicely is an adverb, and its comparative form is more nicely.
fact: «Nicely» means in a pleasant, kind or polite way, as in «ask nicely».
fact: «Nicely» also means well, in a good or satisfactory way, as in «the cake turned out nicely».
fact: In Alice's story, a cat sits «purring so nicely by the fire», which means it is purring in a calm, pleasant way.
fact: «We must do this again soon!» is a polite phrase to end a visit nicely; it is not a firm plan.
exercise: «Strict parents often find a middle way if you ask nicely.» What does ask nicely mean? | Ask without saying anything | *Ask with please and a kind voice | Ask in a polite, pleasant way | Ask as loudly as you can
exercise: «The cake turned out nicely.» What does nicely mean here? | Badly and slowly | Angrily | *Well, in a good way | Quietly, behind the door
exercise: «We must do this again soon!» is a polite phrase to end a visit nicely. Why is it not a firm plan? | It is a secret code | It is the start of a long journey | It is a plan written in ink | *It is a polite way to say goodbye, not a promise
test: «The dog walked nicely beside its owner, without pulling.» What does nicely suggest? | *Calmly and politely | Barking at every bird | Sleeping under the table | Running wildly ahead
test: Ben says, «My project is doing nicely.» What does he mean? | *It is going well | It is very loud | It is finished and broken | It is in the bin
exam: «Alice's cat sat purring so nicely by the fire.» Which word has the same meaning as nicely here? | *Pleasantly | Loudly | Hungrily | Angrily
